# ==============================================================================
# Processor env template — copy to `.env` and fill in real values. Never commit .env.
#
# The full key set mirrors the processor's env contract — config.ts, ctp-region.ts,
# env-store-settings.ts, encryption-key-guard.ts, public-url-guard.ts, store-key.ts and
# resolve-store-config.ts iterating the provider manifest's credentialEnvKeys
# (processor/src/infrastructure/config, providers/psp/psp-module.ts) — and connect.yaml.
# On-prem uses the identical contract (deployment/onprem/.env-sample).
# ==============================================================================

# --- commercetools Composable Commerce API client -----------------------------
# Required scopes (connect.yaml): manage_payments, manage_orders, view_sessions,
# manage_checkout_payment_intents, introspect_oauth_tokens, manage_types, view_types,
# manage_states (the eight PaymentState states post-deploy registers for the payment
# state the connector writes — without it the deploy fails on a 403), view_stores
# (store-existence authorization + reference data), view_project_settings (reference
# data), manage_key_value_documents (the config and runtime Custom Objects), and
# view_customers (the signed-in shopper's date of birth, which buy-now-pay-later
# methods require).
CTP_PROJECT_KEY=[composable-commerce-project-key]
CTP_CLIENT_ID=[composable-commerce-client-id]
CTP_CLIENT_SECRET=[composable-commerce-client-secret]

# --- commercetools region ({cloudRegion}.{cloudProvider}, e.g. europe-west1.gcp) ---
# The six commercetools URLs (auth/api/session/checkout + the MC-API jwks/jwtIssuer used
# for Merchant JWT validation) are DERIVED from this one token. Merchant JWTs are REAL
# Merchant Center JWTs (no mock issuer in any environment, local development included):
# the only acceptable bearer is an exchange token minted by the MC
# API Gateway /proxy/forward-to (60s).
CTP_REGION=europe-west1.gcp

# --- Service tuning ------------------------------------------------------------
# Timeout (ms) for the /operations/status downstream health check. Default 5000.
HEALTH_CHECK_TIMEOUT=5000
# Winston log level: error | warn | info | debug. Default info.
LOGGER_LEVEL=info

# --- Store-level authorization (SEC hardening) ---------------------------------
# The MC permission an operator must hold on EVERY merchant /operations endpoint is a BRAND
# value (providers/psp/brand.defaults.json `managePermission`, which must be set to
# canManage<TitleCase(ENTRY_POINT_URI_PATH)> for the entry point the mc and mc-view applications
# are deployed under, or every config mutation answers 403) — NOT a deployment env var.
# It authorizes two things, and
# the second MOVES REAL MONEY: the store connection (read/write the store config, testconnection,
# upload-logo, disconnect) AND the Merchant Center payment panel, whose intents CAPTURE, REFUND
# and CANCEL. Grant it only to the MC Teams you trust to act on payments — the operator's MC
# Team must be GRANTED that permission, else the gateway mints a token carrying no
# user_permissions claim and the gate fails closed. The /operations config endpoints also verify
# the effective store key (X-Store-Key header, else the project key) resolves to a REAL project
# store and reject an unknown store 403 (needs the view_stores scope).

# --- Unzer credentials ----------------------------------------------------------
# NOT an environment variable. The Unzer public/private API key pair is entered per store in the
# Merchant Center application and stored encrypted in the unzer-connector-config Custom Object.

# --- Encryption keyring - SECRET (connect.yaml securedConfiguration) -------------
# AES-256-GCM key (64 hex chars used raw, otherwise SHA-256-derived) — the CURRENT key of the
# encryption keyring. New ciphertext is written under it in the v1 key-id envelope
# (v1:<key-id>:<iv>:<tag>:<ciphertext>, key-id = short SHA-256 fingerprint of the key). It encrypts
# the secret fields of the per-store unzer-connector-config Custom Object. REQUIRED: the processor
# and post-deploy both refuse to run without it. The boot guard also
# refuses a WEAK value — a placeholder (this bracketed seed included) or anything under 32
# characters — because the webhook capability-URL token is derived from this key. Generate with:
# openssl rand -hex 32
ENCRYPTION_KEY=<openssl rand -hex 32>
# OPTIONAL previous key of the encryption keyring — set it to enable zero-downtime rotation.
# Decryption selects the key whose fingerprint matches the envelope key-id, falling back to this
# previous key; new ciphertext is always written under the current ENCRYPTION_KEY. When set,
# post-deploy re-encrypts existing unzer-connector-config secrets under the current key AND
# re-registers every credentialed store environment's webhook subscription with the current-key
# capability URL (best-effort, idempotent). Leave unset when not rotating.
ENCRYPTION_KEY_PREVIOUS=

# --- PSP deployment config -------------------------------------------------------
# The vendor API host (test and live), the integrator identifier and the telemetry header name
# are BRAND values (providers/psp/brand.defaults.json: `defaultHost` / `defaultHostLive`,
# `integrator`, `telemetryHeaderName`) — NOT env vars. SANDBOX vs LIVE is picked by the resolved
# store's mode, and the active environment block's `host` overrides both per store.
# The webhook URL is DERIVED, not configured: {processor origin}/webhooks/{storeKey}/{token} — the
# origin comes from the request's Host header (or, in the post-deploy, from the URL Connect assigned)
# and the token is a MAC derived from ENCRYPTION_KEY. A per-store `webhookUrl` override in the
# environment block wins VERBATIM, so it must embed a valid token itself. Unzer POSTs lifecycle
# events there, so the processor must be reachable from Unzer.

# --- Return leg ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The processor's OWN public return endpoint base (the connector's `/return` route) is DERIVED:
# {processor origin}/return. createPayment appends `?ctPaymentId=<id>` and hands that
# to the PSP as the redirect target, so the return leg can authenticate the callback against the
# payment id it stamped, then reflect the definitive status.
# Return-leg hardening (SEC-M1 / CR-M3). Comma-separated allowlist of permitted storefront
# ORIGINS (scheme + host [+ port]) a shopper return URL may target; a return URL whose origin
# is not listed is rejected at intake and never used for a 302. EMPTY/unset fails CLOSED
# (a supplied return URL is rejected).
#
# For local development this list must ALSO carry the enabler dev server's origin, because both
# browser surfaces served from it — the QA console `test-console.html` and the demo shop
# `demo-shop.html` — post `returnUrl = window.location.href`, and an origin that is not listed
# makes `POST /payments` fail at intake before any vendor call. That origin is
# `http://localhost:3000` by default and `https://localhost:3000` when the enabler runs with
# `VITE_DEV_HTTPS=1` (see `enabler/.env.template`); list both if you switch between them, e.g.
# PSP_ALLOWED_RETURN_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,https://localhost:3000
PSP_ALLOWED_RETURN_ORIGINS=https://your-shop.example.com
# The single safe sink the return leg redirects to on ANY failure (unknown payment,
# missing stamped payment id, off-allowlist/absent shopper URL). REQUIRED for the
# return leg — the shopper is never 500'd and payment existence stays unobservable.
PSP_RETURN_FAILURE_URL=https://your-shop.example.com/checkout/payment-failed

# --- Vendor transport ----------------------------------------------------------
# The single-vendor-call timeout is a HARDCODED constant (30000 ms) in the connector, not a
# deployment knob. At that deadline the call fails; a timeout is AMBIGUOUS — the vendor may have
# performed the operation and never answered — so the reserved amount stays fenced off instead of
# being released. The connector's Unzer client enforces it on the vendor socket (a per-call
# AbortController deadline that raises an AMBIGUOUS 504, never a 4xx). The merchant panel's
# reconciliation window is DERIVED from it (this bound + 5 minutes).

# --- Vendor identity -------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendor identity lives in providers/psp/brand.defaults.json (displayName, paymentInterface,
# telemetryHeaderName, integrator, shoppingCartExtension, customObjectContainer,
# paymentMethodsContainer, webhookMarkerContainer, defaultHost / defaultHostLive, an optional
# backOffice { test, live } pair, managePermission, paymentTypeKey - the commercetools custom-Type
# key). That file is maintained by hand; there are no BRAND_* env overrides for any of these values.
